.TH RENAME 3
.SH NAME
rename \- change the name of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
int
rename(from, to)
char *from, *to;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rename
gives the file named
.I from
the name
.IR to .
If a file named
.I to
already exists, it is removed first, unless it is a directory. If
.I from
and
.I to
are names of the same file, nothing is done.
.PP
XENIX has no rename system call. rename makes the new name with
.BR link (2)
and then removes the old one with
.BR unlink (2),
as
.BR mv (1)
does; for a moment the file has both names. Both names must therefore be
in the same file system.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
0 on success; \-1 on failure, with errno set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 10
.B ENOENT
.I from
does not exist, or a directory in
.I to
does not.
.TP
.B EXDEV
The two names are in different file systems.
.TP
.B EISDIR
.I to
is a directory.
.TP
.B EACCES
A directory cannot be searched, or written to make or remove a name.
.SH SEE ALSO
mv(1), link(2), unlink(2)
.SH HISTORY
rename is a system call in 4.2BSD. Version 7 AT&T UNIX and System V
have none.
